    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d855">

                <pb facs="0949" n="847" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg847"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/745: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-28T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 28, 1919,
                                3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your July 7, 11 a.m. Department has received note from Minister of Salvador in
                        Washington<anchor n="15" xml:id="d855-f1"/> informing it that Salvador had
                    suggested to Governments of Central America that joint action might be taken
                    with beneficial result in order to secure peace in Costa Rica.</p>
                <p>Department has informed Minister of Salvador that this plan, which seems to be in
                    harmony with the spirit of the Washington Conventions, has been regarded by the
                    Department with sympathetic interest.</p>
                <p>You may informally inform Minister for Foreign Affairs that this Government
                    considers the answer made to Salvador by the Nicaraguan Government regarding the
                    suggestion of Salvador, to be a proper one.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d855-f1" n="15" xml:id="d855-f1-content">
